Package: debian-minerva
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: cage, chromium | firefox-esr
Suggests: weston
Description: Debian Minerva desktop environment (Rust session + shell)
 Minerva is a desktop environment for Debian: a dependency-free Rust session
 daemon owns the desktop state (windows, virtual desktops, notifications,
 theming, virtual filesystem, terminal) and a kiosk shell renders it as a
 full screen session.
 .
 Installing this package adds a "Minerva" entry to the display manager
 (GDM, LightDM, SDDM). Selecting it at login starts the session: the daemon
 is supervised on loopback with a per-session token and a kiosk compositor
 (cage on Wayland, or the existing X display) shows the desktop.
 .
 Features: virtual desktops, dock, app launcher with 18 built-in apps,
 quick settings, notification shade, window manager with edge snapping,
 light/dark theming with 6 accents and 5 SVG wallpapers, and a Rust-backed
 terminal. No Google services or branding.
